.env.*.local

# Editors
.idea
.vscode
.cursor
.claude
# EVERY CLAUDE.md is a local, per-checkout file — the root one and the
# package-level ones (packages/react, apps/web) alike. They are the
# maintainer's agent-facing notes: they churn on every round and the churn
# dominated review, which is the same reason `/docs/` below is local.
#
# Deliberately NOT anchored, unlike `/docs/`: this pattern matches a FILE of
# that exact name, so it can never swallow a directory the way an unanchored
# `docs/` swallowed the docs site. The one thing to keep in mind is the mirror
# of that hazard — a new package's CLAUDE.md is ignored without anyone saying
# so, which is the intent here.
CLAUDE.md

# Agent-facing engine documentation (architecture notes, the diagnostics flag
# reference, the device-campaign postmortems). Local per-checkout, same as the
# root CLAUDE.md above: it churns on every motion round and the churn dominated
# review. Source comments still cite these paths — they are the maintainer's
# working notes, and the code comments they cite remain the primary source.
#
# ROOT-ANCHORED, and it must stay that way. An unanchored `docs/` matches a
# directory of that name at ANY depth, which swallowed the docs SITE
# (apps/web/app/[lang]/docs) — and because Tailwind's source scanner honors
# .gitignore, its classes stopped being generated: the sidebar's `md:block`
# vanished from the bundle and the aside stayed `display: none`, failing the
# docs e2e specs with a build that compiled cleanly.
/docs/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Logs
*.log
*storybook.log
firebase-debug.log

# Coverage
coverage

